WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.184 --> 00:00:01.283
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.283 --> 00:00:05.434
today's message is ignore
the opinions of others.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.467
Over to you, Paul Thomas Anderson.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.862
(rooster crowing)

00:00:09.862 --> 00:00:12.178
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.190
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:18.865
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:18.865 --> 00:00:21.017
- The one thing I always remember thinking

00:00:21.017 --> 00:00:23.509
initially when I was trying to make films,

00:00:23.509 --> 00:00:25.601
you always felt like,

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.731
you got nervous that
somebody else was right

00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:28.564
when they were talking to you,

00:00:28.564 --> 00:00:30.169
you know, who maybe was
in a position of power,

00:00:30.169 --> 00:00:33.746
like that their opinion somehow was right,

00:00:33.746 --> 00:00:35.943
or better than yours,

00:00:35.943 --> 00:00:38.249
you could never stop to think,

00:00:38.249 --> 00:00:39.244
"No, it's just different,

00:00:39.244 --> 00:00:42.009
"you just think differently
than I do, and that's okay.

00:00:42.009 --> 00:00:43.109
"But I'm not wrong."

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.670
Soon you can get filled with such fear,

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.393
and it's really easy to
just get your heart broken

00:00:50.393 --> 00:00:52.061
and kind of, sort of beaten,

00:00:52.061 --> 00:00:55.644
as you're sort of
attempting to make films,

00:00:56.971 --> 00:00:59.774
it's a miracle any time
any one of them gets made.

00:00:59.774 --> 00:01:01.237
It's a miracle.

00:01:01.237 --> 00:01:03.556
And it's a miracle
every time, I feel like.

00:01:03.556 --> 00:01:05.509
It's a miracle every time
a scene kind of gets done

00:01:05.509 --> 00:01:07.905
and through the birth canal and done.

00:01:07.905 --> 00:01:09.896
I mean it's never any less of a miracle

00:01:09.896 --> 00:01:11.729
or any less difficult.

00:01:17.555 --> 00:01:19.972
There just should be no fear,

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.533
I just always remember
kind of being pummeled

00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:23.998
by fear early on and feeling like,

00:01:23.998 --> 00:01:27.409
"God if I could've just gotten
rid of that fear earlier,

00:01:27.409 --> 00:01:29.646
"this might've been a little bit easier."

00:01:29.646 --> 00:01:31.274
It's just, don't give a (beep),

00:01:31.274 --> 00:01:33.070
that's kind of the best thing to do.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.551
- Not one ounce of my self-worth comes

00:01:35.551 --> 00:01:37.825
from your opinion of me.

00:01:37.825 --> 00:01:40.670
Not one ounce of my self-worth

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.973
comes from your opinion of me.

00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:44.747
I think it's really important

00:01:44.747 --> 00:01:46.276
to be able to separate

00:01:46.276 --> 00:01:49.243
your value as a human being

00:01:49.243 --> 00:01:51.195
from what other people think.

00:01:51.195 --> 00:01:53.270
Because if you're
constantly being impacted

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.648
by other people's impressions
and ideas and opinions,

00:01:56.648 --> 00:01:58.151
then you're never going to be you.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.424
'Cause people always have
a direction for your life.

00:02:00.424 --> 00:02:02.337
If you don't come up
with your own life plan,

00:02:02.337 --> 00:02:04.163
I guarantee the people around you

00:02:04.163 --> 00:02:07.259
will create your life plan for you,

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:10.263
through their eyes, through their lens.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:13.156
And they can't ultimately
give you what you need.

00:02:13.156 --> 00:02:15.392
I swear, the most valuable
things that you can learn,

00:02:15.392 --> 00:02:17.711
not just as an entrepreneur,
but as a human being,

00:02:17.711 --> 00:02:19.664
is to separate yourself,

00:02:19.664 --> 00:02:20.497
and your value,

00:02:20.497 --> 00:02:22.276
from what somebody else thinks about you.

00:02:22.276 --> 00:02:23.359
And I've told this story before,

00:02:23.359 --> 00:02:26.175
but I think it's worth
sharing again on this video

00:02:26.175 --> 00:02:27.843
about the little man.

00:02:27.843 --> 00:02:29.757
The little man's a concept in the book,

00:02:29.757 --> 00:02:33.971
and the little man's a
person who just hates.

00:02:33.971 --> 00:02:35.846
The little man is the person who tells you

00:02:35.846 --> 00:02:38.162
all the reasons why it's
not going to work out.

00:02:38.162 --> 00:02:39.713
The little man is the person who maybe

00:02:39.713 --> 00:02:41.791
took their shot once,
and they didn't succeed,

00:02:41.791 --> 00:02:43.865
and so they have to bring
everybody else down.

00:02:43.865 --> 00:02:44.718
'Cause they don't want to go out

00:02:44.718 --> 00:02:46.496
and do something amazing with their life,

00:02:46.496 --> 00:02:48.000
and the only satisfaction they get is

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.214
when they can bring other
people down to their level.

00:02:50.214 --> 00:02:51.309
They want to be above,

00:02:51.309 --> 00:02:54.209
and so they need to crush
everyone else around them,

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:55.867
and they do it by tearing others down

00:02:55.867 --> 00:02:57.739
instead of building up their own thing.

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:00.221
And the little man came to me

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:03.380
when I was making one of my
biggest videos of all time.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.562
But at the start, I didn't
know it was going to work out.

00:03:05.562 --> 00:03:07.236
I had this video around Believe,

00:03:07.236 --> 00:03:09.348
it was my first Believe video,

00:03:09.348 --> 00:03:11.018
I just found my one word, Believe,

00:03:11.018 --> 00:03:13.249
I wanted to make a video about it,

00:03:13.249 --> 00:03:15.877
and we made this video that's
six and a half minutes long.

00:03:15.877 --> 00:03:17.872
And I showed it to a guy
who was in the industry,

00:03:17.872 --> 00:03:20.898
it's not just showing it
to some high school friend.

00:03:20.898 --> 00:03:21.888
If they didn't like it,

00:03:21.888 --> 00:03:24.407
it's easy to reject that opinion and say,

00:03:24.407 --> 00:03:26.255
"Well you don't even know
what you're talking about."

00:03:26.255 --> 00:03:29.010
But he was in the industry,
he was in the video industry.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.170
And he looked at it and he said,

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:34.745
"No YouTube video should
be six minutes long,

00:03:34.745 --> 00:03:38.031
"tell me you actually understand
how the internet works."

00:03:38.031 --> 00:03:39.863
Some of the quotes are in the book.

00:03:39.863 --> 00:03:43.039
And the younger version of me

00:03:43.039 --> 00:03:44.984
might have listed to him.

00:03:44.984 --> 00:03:47.118
Might have said, "Hmm, here's
some guy who's an expert,

00:03:47.118 --> 00:03:48.293
"who knows what he's talking about,

00:03:48.293 --> 00:03:50.941
"maybe I should listen to
his advice and not do it."

00:03:50.941 --> 00:03:53.585
But when I watched the video myself,

00:03:53.585 --> 00:03:55.861
it just made me come alive,

00:03:55.861 --> 00:03:57.201
it just made me so excited,

00:03:57.201 --> 00:03:59.602
it got my blood pumping, I loved it.

00:03:59.602 --> 00:04:01.349
And I couldn't imagine stripping

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:02.931
four and a half minutes out of it,

00:04:02.931 --> 00:04:07.772
just to make it fit this
guy's two minute timeline.

00:04:07.772 --> 00:04:11.193
And so I decided, you
know what, forget you,

00:04:11.193 --> 00:04:13.223
I'm just going to do it
and see what happens.

00:04:13.223 --> 00:04:16.481
And it quickly became the most
popular video on the channel.

00:04:16.481 --> 00:04:19.043
My best video to that point
had a hundred thousand views,

00:04:19.043 --> 00:04:21.238
my best video took me a year to get that,

00:04:21.238 --> 00:04:24.202
this video hit a hundred thousand
views in the first month.

00:04:24.202 --> 00:04:25.995
And now it's over two million views.

00:04:25.995 --> 00:04:28.794
And so, it's great to
listen to the opinions

00:04:28.794 --> 00:04:30.879
of other people just to get feedback.

00:04:30.879 --> 00:04:31.860
But at the end of the day,

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.017
it's up to you to make that decision.

00:04:34.017 --> 00:04:36.543
Does it feel right for you?

00:04:36.543 --> 00:04:38.534
And not to live your life only according

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:40.245
to the expectations of other people.

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:42.799
And if you don't do what
they want you to do,

00:04:42.799 --> 00:04:45.209
suddenly you feel less worth

00:04:45.209 --> 00:04:46.389
because they're attacking you

00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:47.698
saying you should've done it.

00:04:47.698 --> 00:04:50.477
Not one ounce of my self worth comes

00:04:50.477 --> 00:04:52.835
from your opinion of me.

00:04:52.835 --> 00:04:55.424
Embracing that and believing that

00:04:55.424 --> 00:04:58.921
will help you build your
version of your life

00:04:58.921 --> 00:05:01.722
instead of letting other
people dictate your plans.

00:05:01.722 --> 00:05:03.796
So the question today is I'm curious,

00:05:03.796 --> 00:05:05.910
I want to hear your little man story.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.862
I want to hear a story
of somebody in your life

00:05:07.862 --> 00:05:09.040
who tried to hold you back,

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.636
tell you you can't do something,

00:05:10.636 --> 00:05:13.402
and maybe it worked, or
maybe you said no to them,

00:05:13.402 --> 00:05:15.636
I want to hear your little man story.

00:05:15.636 --> 00:05:17.017
Leave in the comments below,

00:05:17.017 --> 00:05:18.642
and we'll join in the discussion.

00:05:18.642 --> 00:05:19.656
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:05:19.656 --> 00:05:22.506
to Marsha McGuire from waterbirdcalls.com,

00:05:22.506 --> 00:05:23.930
thank you so much Marsha for picking up

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.122
a copy of my book, Your One Word,

00:05:26.122 --> 00:05:27.992
it really really really means a lot to me,

00:05:27.992 --> 00:05:29.458
and I hope you'll enjoy it.

00:05:29.458 --> 00:05:30.959
Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:05:30.959 --> 00:05:32.103
I believe in you,

00:05:32.103 --> 00:05:34.058
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:05:34.058 --> 00:05:36.006
and whatever your one word is,

00:05:36.006 --> 00:05:37.350
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.500
for another shot of Ent-spresso.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.270
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:45.967
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:05:45.967 --> 00:05:46.800
Hi Believe Nation,

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.860
if you want to go a little
bit deeper into this topic

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.818
and learn more and get more context,

00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:52.974
I'm adding in some extra bonus clips

00:05:52.974 --> 00:05:55.209
that I think you'll enjoy.

00:05:55.209 --> 00:05:56.713
- [Interviewer] You don't pay
a lot of attention to reviews,

00:05:56.713 --> 00:05:58.118
and those kind of things?

00:05:58.118 --> 00:06:03.113
- Well, you know, you're
always affected by opinion

00:06:03.113 --> 00:06:06.946
but the more opinions
there are of you, of me,

00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:10.436
the less I look at them.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.427
Because I just can't
live my life based upon

00:06:12.427 --> 00:06:14.334
what other people think about me.

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:15.918
So I can't concern myself too much

00:06:15.918 --> 00:06:17.257
with what other people think,

00:06:17.257 --> 00:06:19.010
you know, it's just not healthy.

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:21.860
I don't think I could
continue to do what I do

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.367
if I was constantly worrying about

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:25.040
what somebody thought about it.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.154
- How did you ignore all those naysayers

00:06:27.154 --> 00:06:29.188
and continue to sort of
blaze the trail and then--

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:33.300
- Well 90, 95% of all new ventures fail.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:36.141
So if you just bet
against all new ventures,

00:06:36.141 --> 00:06:40.737
odds are 90% that you're going
to be right, 90% of the time.

00:06:40.737 --> 00:06:44.114
But, you're going to
miss that one out of ten,

00:06:44.114 --> 00:06:48.991
or one out of twenty chances
to really hit a home run.

00:06:48.991 --> 00:06:52.324
And I wasn't worried about the naysayers

00:06:53.299 --> 00:06:54.585
saying it wasn't going to work,

00:06:54.585 --> 00:06:58.532
I just laughed about it,
because I knew it was.

00:06:58.532 --> 00:06:59.997
- And you worked very hard at it as well.

00:06:59.997 --> 00:07:02.148
- I wasn't going to let it fail.

00:07:02.148 --> 00:07:06.965
And even, if you read my
book, it's right there.

00:07:06.965 --> 00:07:08.542
I wasn't going to let it fail.

00:07:08.542 --> 00:07:11.459
And I'm not going to let humanity fail

00:07:12.324 --> 00:07:14.824
to get rid of nuclear weapons,

00:07:16.355 --> 00:07:17.432
and handle this energy thing.

00:07:17.432 --> 00:07:20.720
I'm going to keep fighting
till we start getting it right.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:23.606
- Ignore people telling
you your idea is bad.

00:07:23.606 --> 00:07:25.452
They may be right, but
the only way to know

00:07:25.452 --> 00:07:27.160
is to actually build it out.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:31.311
And I think the thing that
works about Silicon Valley

00:07:31.311 --> 00:07:32.659
that's different than Mexico City

00:07:32.659 --> 00:07:34.607
or almost anywhere else in the world

00:07:34.607 --> 00:07:37.693
is the default response if someone says,

00:07:37.693 --> 00:07:38.869
"Hey, I'm going to start a start-up,

00:07:38.869 --> 00:07:39.843
"here's my idea."

00:07:39.843 --> 00:07:42.324
The default response is to be excited,

00:07:42.324 --> 00:07:44.963
and think like "Oh, why might that work?"

00:07:44.963 --> 00:07:46.670
And in most of the rest of the world,

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:49.024
The default response when
you tell someone your idea

00:07:49.024 --> 00:07:51.512
is to say "Oh, that's not going to work."

00:07:51.512 --> 00:07:54.487
And this is really toxic for start-ups.

00:07:54.487 --> 00:07:56.523
'Cause you have to believe in yourself.

00:07:56.523 --> 00:07:59.164
And good ideas, because
they sound like bad ideas,

00:07:59.164 --> 00:08:02.623
are so fragile and so kill-able,

00:08:02.623 --> 00:08:04.139
that you have to be really careful

00:08:04.139 --> 00:08:06.175
to insulate yourself against this.

